    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nAfter `:restart`, nvim forgets options set by `-d` command line option, such as `'diff'`.\nThis bisects to 845b66dd4a50d7b54050990e27919549c331e1bb (#40321).\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```\nnvim -d --clean foo bar\n:set diff?  \" diff\n:bw\n:restart\n\" window is not split\n:set diff?  \" nodiff\n```\n\nand `scrollbind`, `cursorbind`, `nowrap`, etc are unset.\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`:restart` does not discard diff-mode and options set by command line option `-d`.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-887+g12ea9735f\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nn/a\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nEndeavourOS\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1-arch2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
